  <static seed="651" source="Library/Rochester/setVectorCalculus2/ur_vc_12_1.pg">
    <statement><p>For each of the following vector fields <alert> F </alert>, decide whether it is
conservative or not by computing curl <alert> F </alert>. Type in a potential function
f (that is, <m>\nabla f = \mathbf{F}</m>). If it is not conservative, type N.</p>
<p>A. <m>\mathbf{F} \left( x, y \right) = \left( -14 x + 5 y \right) \mathbf{i} +
\left( 5 x + 4 y \right) \mathbf{j}</m></p>
<p><m>f \left( x, y \right) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>B. <m>\mathbf{F} \left( x, y \right) = -7 y \mathbf{i}  - 6 x \mathbf{j}</m></p>
<p><m>f \left( x, y \right) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>C. <m>\mathbf{F} \left( x, y, z \right) = -7 x \mathbf{i}  - 6 y \mathbf{j} + \mathbf{k}</m></p>
<p><m>f \left( x, y, z \right) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>D. <m>\mathbf{F} \left( x, y \right) = \left( -7 \sin y \right) \mathbf{i} +
\left( 10 y  - 7 x \cos y \right) \mathbf{j}</m></p>
<p><m>f \left( x, y \right) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>E. <m>\mathbf{F} \left( x, y, z \right) = -7 x^{2} \mathbf{i} +
5 y^{2} \mathbf{j} + 2 z^{2} \mathbf{k}</m></p>
<p><m>f \left( x, y, z \right) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p>Note: Your answers should be either expressions of x, y and z (e.g. <lq/>3xy +
2yz<rq/>), or
the letter <lq/>N<rq/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-7x^{2}+5xy+2y^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{N}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-7x^{2}}{2}+\frac{\left(-7+1\right)y^{2}}{2}+z</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-7x\sin\mathopen{}\left(y\right)+5y^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{1}{3}\mathopen{}\left(-7x^{3}+5y^{3}+2z^{3}\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
